      text: "In any group setting, it is common [1] one or two members to contribute less effort than everyone else. Sometimes this happens by accident, but other times it is a deliberate strategy [2] as weaponized incompetence. People who use this strategy often pretend to struggle with simple tasks [3] someone else will eventually take over. [4] left unaddressed, this pattern can quietly damage trust among teammates over time. Experts suggest that clear communication and firm boundaries are usually more effective [5] silently accepting extra work.",
