    wordBank: {
      words: ["(A) accountability", "(B) burden", "(C) collaboration", "(D) delegate", "(E) dynamic", "(F) fairness", "(G) initiative", "(H) morale", "(I) teamwork", "(J) workload"],
      passage: "Healthy [1] among coworkers depends on everyone contributing roughly equal effort toward shared goals.\n\nWhen one person consistently avoids [2], frustration can quickly spread among the rest of the team.\n\nManagers who fail to address uneven [3] often watch overall team [4] decline over time, as hardworking employees begin to feel taken advantage of.\n\nOne useful strategy is to clearly [5] specific tasks to each team member from the very beginning of a project.\n\nWhen responsibilities are divided fairly, a sense of [6] naturally develops, since no one feels unfairly burdened.\n\nTeams that regularly discuss workplace [7] openly are often better at catching problems before resentment builds.\n\nShowing genuine [8] by volunteering for difficult tasks can help rebuild trust within a struggling team.\n\nLeaders play an important role in making sure no single person carries an unfair [9], so that everyone's share of the work stays reasonable.\n\nUltimately, lasting [10] requires every member to feel equally responsible for the team's success.",
      answers: { 1: "I", 2: "A", 3: "J", 4: "H", 5: "D", 6: "F", 7: "E", 8: "G", 9: "B", 10: "C" }
    },
