        "Not every case of underperformance in a group is intentional, but one particular pattern stands out as especially frustrating. [1]",
        "This strategy often works because others feel obligated to step in rather than let the task fail. [2] Over time, the person using this strategy learns that pretending to struggle is easier than actually trying. [3]",
