      passage: "Modern styling apps rely on a complex [1] running in the background to process each uploaded photo almost instantly.\n\nBefore making suggestions, the software performs a detailed [2] of lighting, color balance and facial structure.\n\nMany users are surprised by how [3] these results can be, especially compared to older, more subjective methods.\n\nEvery face has a unique [4], the overall tone and texture of the skin that color experts study closely.\n\nBeneath the visible skin tone lies a subtler [5], a cooler or warmer quality that strongly affects which colors look flattering.\n\nOnce the analysis is complete, the app will typically [6] a small group of shades best suited to the user.\n\nSome tools go further and let users [7] their results by adjusting preferences such as favorite colors or styles.\n\nOthers [8] the entire experience even more, remembering past choices to improve future suggestions.\n\nA well-chosen color [9] can make a simple outfit look noticeably more polished.\n\nUltimately, every recommendation still depends on specific facial [10] such as eye color, hair color and skin tone working together.",
